#!/usr/bin/env bash
# OpenCode Cockpit as one file.  Generated by tools/make_oneshot.py from the tracked files of the repository: do not edit.
#
#     bash opencode-cockpit.sh [FOLDER]     write the 107 files into FOLDER (default: opencode-cockpit)
#
# Needs bash, and sha256sum or shasum.  It calls no git and opens no connection, refuses a FOLDER that already holds
# files, writes nothing outside FOLDER, and ends by checking the SHA-256 of every file it wrote.
# Every file below is a plain here-document, so this file can be read before it is run.
set -eu
dest=${1:-opencode-cockpit}
case "$dest" in -*) echo "usage: bash opencode-cockpit.sh [FOLDER]" >&2; exit 2;; esac
if [ -e "$dest" ] && [ -n "$(ls -A "$dest" 2>/dev/null)" ]; then
  echo "opencode-cockpit.sh: $dest already holds files; give a new or empty folder" >&2; exit 2
fi
if command -v sha256sum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sum256() { sha256sum "$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
elif command -v shasum >/dev/null 2>&1; then sum256() { shasum -a 256 "$1" | cut -d' ' -f1; }
else echo "opencode-cockpit.sh: needs sha256sum or shasum to check what it writes" >&2; exit 2; fi
chop() { printf '%s' "$(cat "$1")" > "$1.oc-tmp" && mv "$1.oc-tmp" "$1"; }     # drop the newline a here-document adds
mkdir -p "$dest"; cd "$dest"
mkdir -p '.github/workflows' 'cockpit' 'cockpit/schema' 'icons' 'tests' 'tests/fake_bin' 'tests/format' 'tools' 'web'
cat > '.github/workflows/test.yml' <<'OC_EOF_0'
name: test
on:
  push:
  pull_request:
permissions:
  contents: read
jobs:
  test:
    runs-on: ${{ matrix.os }}
    strategy:
      fail-fast: false
      matrix:
        include:
          - {os: ubuntu-24.04, python: '3.9'}      # the oldest Python this is written for; the newest runner image has no build of it
          - {os: ubuntu-latest, python: '3.12'}
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
        with:
          fetch-depth: 0
      - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
        with:
          python-version: ${{ matrix.python }}
      - name: Tests (standard library only, one file at a time)
        run: |
          for t in tests/test_*.py; do echo "== $t"; python "$t" || exit 1; done
      - name: Icons are what icons/ gives
        run: python tools/make_icons.py --check
      - name: Nothing private in the files or the history
        run: python tools/privacy_scan.py --history
OC_EOF_0
cat > '.gitignore' <<'OC_EOF_1'
runs/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
pro/node_modules
OC_EOF_1
cat > 'ICONS.md' <<'OC_EOF_2'
# Model icons

The page shows a small mark next to every seat, order and launch so that you can see at a glance which model family did
what. Three families have a mark of their own; a model of any other family gets a plain grey hexagon ring.

| Family | Matched in the seat's model id | Source file | SHA-256 |
|---|---|---|---|
| DeepSeek | `deepseek` | `icons/deepseek-color.svg` | `40632a9898779d4ff6186b847f9bf4461925adf89a08a8dae88e5b6de0c64c7a` |
| Kimi | `kimi`, `moonshot` | `icons/kimi-color.svg` | `c1b438a9b311e52c2cc5c8622a7fb59c90d614e6fe2c10a3b5a6aca115674691` |
| Qwen | `qwen`, `dashscope`, `tongyi` | `icons/qwen-color.svg` | `b930916572c9966dddc151d0346bde6527c7012b3070feac763826c1c41585b7` |
| any other | everything else | drawn for this project in `tools/make_icons.py` | - |

## Where the three files come from

They come from the npm package `@lobehub/icons-static-svg`, version 1.104.0
(`icons/deepseek-color.svg`, `icons/kimi-color.svg`, `icons/qwen-color.svg` in that package; project
<https://github.com/lobehub/lobe-icons>). Root attributes use a consistent order and decimal path coordinates are serialized with six fractional places in this repository; their numeric values and shapes are unchanged. The table records the local file hashes. That package is under the MIT licence, Copyright (c) 2023 LobeHub; the licence
text is in `icons/LICENSE` and covers those three files only.

The logos themselves are trademarks of their owners (DeepSeek; Moonshot AI for Kimi; Alibaba Cloud for Qwen). They are
used here only to say which model a seat runs. This project is not affiliated with or endorsed by any of them, nor by
OpenCode or LobeHub.

## How they get into the page

`web/icons.js` is generated, not written by hand:

    python3 tools/make_icons.py            # rebuild web/icons.js from icons/
    python3 tools/make_icons.py --check    # exit 1 when web/icons.js is out of date

The generator takes only path data and fill colours out of a file. A file whose SHA-256 is not the one in the table, or
that holds anything but `<svg>`, `<title>` and `<path d fill>`, is refused. The page then draws each mark with
`createElementNS`; no SVG markup is ever inserted as HTML.

## Adding a family

1. Put the SVG in `icons/` and add a line to `SOURCES` in `tools/make_icons.py` (family, file, display name, SHA-256).
2. Add the family and the pattern that recognises its model ids to `FAMILIES` in `cockpit/live.py`.
3. Run `python3 tools/make_icons.py`, add a row to the table above, and run the tests.
