## Retained text contracts and the exact exceptions

These exceptions are kept in page wrappers, never in format.mjs. Existing behavioral assertions were not relaxed.

| Call sites | Retained spelling and reason |
| --- | --- |
| `seatSummary` totals and spark-bar titles | One-decimal `N.N s`; `assertSeatSummaries` compares the total exactly and requires the spark title's spaced seconds unit. |
| `seatLaunchStrip` ticks; `seatPanel` total; `canvasPanel` ruler/cursor; `timelineView` ticks and duration labels | Numeric labels agree with fixed-decimal `data-seat-tick`, `data-seat-seconds`, `data-gantt-tick`, `data-gantt-cursor`, `data-timeline-tick`, start and end values. `assertTimeline` pins bar titles; `assertWorkspace` requires spaced seconds. Those values and the related visible units stay unchanged. |
| `seatPanel` launch rows | `N.N s` and `Seconds unavailable` are explicitly asserted by `assertSeatFocus`. |
| `replayBar` text and aria-valuetext | Exact `29.0 s of 29.0 s` style is pinned by `assertReplayWorkspace`; it also agrees with the 0.1-second range control. |
| `canvasView`, `fullSeatPanel`, `launchesView` costs | Four decimals such as `$0.1250`; `assertWorkspace` and `assertLaunchCards` compare exact text. `money` would round these to cents, so these use num-guarded fixedNumber. |
| `launchCards` cost | Raw positive amount, including tiny amounts, is pinned by `assertLaunchCards` as `$` plus the original numeric string. `recordedNumber` validates the number but preserves that spelling. |
| `launchCards` seconds; `launchesView` seconds | Fixed seconds are pinned by `assertLaunchCards` and the live-clock assertions (`2.0`, `3.0`, `7.0`). |
| `runTiles`, `metricsView` elapsed time | `6.0 s` and `6.0` are pinned together for the same backend wall time. |
| `teamStats` seconds | Fixed `N.N s` is pinned by `assertTeamStats`. |
| `launchDurationChart` aggregate title | `assertSummaryCharts` pins the prefix `Launch durations in seconds:`. Its numeric samples keep the original three-decimal seconds; individual point tooltips use durationSec. |
| `launchesView` token pair | Exact raw input/output pair is pinned, including `-1 / 1` in the negative-input fixture. `recordedNumber` preserves that legacy hyphen minus. Other counts use the spec's true minus. |
| `resultsView`, `canvasPanel` byte receipts | Exact raw `37 B`, `rev 2 / 37 B`, etc. are pinned by results/workspace assertions. The normal Files rows use bytes with decimal scaling and NBSP. |
| `drawView` Files byte-total statistic | `assertViewSummaries` compares `String(sum)` and exercises a missing file size: it explicitly expects `NaN`. `recordedByteTotal` preserves only this inherited NaN exception; normal totals use count. The shared formatter never emits NaN. Removing this exception requires changing that inherited assertion. |
| `countText` use sentences; `libraryHistory` repeated records | Preserve `used once`, `used 0 times`, `recorded twice` and irregular/invariant nouns. Other counts go through plural. Existing helper/Library assertions pin this wording. |
| `shortHex` | First eight hex characters plus ellipsis, and only one ellipsis when a length limit also applies, are pinned by `test_state_words_and_long_hex_have_one_display_boundary`. It delegates grapheme truncation then removes earlier ellipses only when the outer truncation occurs. Full original text remains in the title. |
| `canvasTransform` zoom | The allowed zoom range is 30–150 percent. Format the numeric part with count and retain the percent sign; percent/ratioPercent clamp to 100 and cannot represent the existing zoom contract. Geometry and scale attributes stay raw. |
| `dateLabel`, `weekday`, `clockTime`, `timestampISO` | Absolute calendar headings and wall-clock times have different semantics from relative dayLabel and elapsed clock. These wrappers use label/count/pad2/num/toMs for components, retaining the calendar's UTC headings and local wall-clock display. Library dates use dayLabel with backend time and explicit UTC offset zero. |

