| `showPreview`, `renderEntry`, `diffView`, `launchesView`, `workSentence`, form feedback | File contents, source lines, JSON evidence, backend reasons, user drafts and messages remain verbatim data. They are not reinterpreted as numbers or statuses merely because they contain digits. |
| ISO dates from backend (`dayLink`, Calendar/Day keys, entry time titles/datetime); `parseDate`, `shiftDay`, `shiftMonth` | Preserve identifiers and already serialized date strings. Numeric timestamps use the timestamp/clock wrappers; Library's visible date text uses when. |
| Static headings, button copy, explanatory sentences and state prose | Literal copy is not a conversion from a backend numeric or status value. Dynamic status lookup uses label/stateLabel; existing descriptive sentences remain intact. |
| All CSS | Formatting only; no style changes or screenshots in this pass. |

